Long story then stats below :)
First ascension for me... also no polymorph or genocide used.

Erri had a good feeling as she descended into the dungeon.  Sure,
she'd lost hundreds of friends who though they would be the one to
liberate the amulet from Moloch but she had something on her side that
they didn't.  Or at least that's what she told herself as she shivered
in fright and descended.

Life proved unexpectedly bountiful early on when she discovered a suit
of silver dragon scale mail barely four levels into the dungeon. 
There was a pile of goodies with this armor but she shied away from
taking anything else when her pet wouldn't step on anything.

Feeling like Tyr was truly on her side since he had provided the fine
suit of armor she hurried into the mines.  It was easy pickings down
to the town where she was excited to discover a priest of Tyr giving a
sermon in the temple.  Sacrificing many creatures to her god she was
thrilled to receive Mjollnir as a gift.  She promised to use it
wisely...

After retrieving a pretty grey stone from the bottom of the mines she
returned to the town and donated some money to the priest.  Tyr seemed
happy and granted her some protection.  Then she happily dipped her
long-sword into a fountain.  A hand reached out and before she knew it
she was wielding the mighty sword Excalibur!  Unfortunately the town
watch didn't take kindly to this action and a captain attacked her
mercilessly.  Flying into a mindless rage she didn't calm down until
all the watch were hacked to pieces.  Feeling a little guilty, and a
lot loss acuity in her mind, she tried to atone by praying to Tyr.

Her beloved god wasn't having any of it after her chaotic actions and
he swiftly took away her protection and drained her level for her
impudence.  Sobbing on the steps of the temple she was taken unawares
by a gigantic Yeti that had become lost in the mines.  Slaying it
quickly with her mighty hammer Mjollnir she rushed inside (as quickly
as she could bearing the weight of the corpse) and sacrificed the
creature.  Sure enough Tyr was mollified and she left the mines in a
happy mood again.

A little later teleportitis kicked in after she ate some leprechaun
meat.  This was all good since her ring of teleport control let her
choose where to go.  Unfortunately she managed to faint from hunger
whilst in a shop, after picking something up... and the shopkeeper had
the nerve to accuse her of being a thief after she randomly teleported
out.  Not willing to take that kind of abuse from a shopkeeper she
swiftly slew the kops and then finished off the owner.  That lost her
the strange mental acuity for a second time.  Thankfully another eye
turned up and soon she regained her extra senses.

A few interesting graves of former adventurers yielded a wide array of
potions and scrolls and one had a weapon called Magicbane.  She picked
it up thinking it looked pretty and put it in her bag, promptly
forgetting about it for the rest of her adventures.  A few wishes
granted her a nice cloak and helmet along with some boots of speed. 
Sure enough she discovered an identical cloak one level deeper and 3
pairs of boots within the next 5 levels of descent.  One more wish
went to an amulet of life-saving, after all she wasn't really sure of
herself yet.

Her ring of levitation saw her to the Medusa and blindness enabled her
to swing her newly wielded excalibur and silver saber straight to the
snaked-headed woman's heart.  The castle was deserted by now (since
she had already been down before killing Medusa) and so she grabbed a
few gems.  Exploring the valley of the dead lead her into Gehennom. 
At this point she decided perhaps discretion was the better part of
valor and headed back up the dungeon.

Clearing out Ludios proved simple and the funds acquired were donated
to the priest in minetown for a sizable chunk of protection.  The
quest given her by the Norns proved to be a walkover after the terrors
in the valley of the dead and she soon emerged triumphant with the orb
of fate and a pretty silver bell.

Feeling ready she descended into Gehennom.  Things were going
smoothly, demon princes were being dispatched and mazes solved when
she descended into a strange swamp.  Suddenly engulfed by Juiblex she
felt ill and quickly mashed her way out of the vile creature using her
twin swords.  Praying to Tyr was a big mistake however... Not only did
her prayers not get through they were intercepted by Moloch.  She
laughed as lightning bounced off her then screamed as a disintigration
ray destroyed her cloak and took away her amulet of life-saving.  Her
last wish went to another amulet which she hastily wore.

Mourning the loss of her protection from Tyr she was a little more
cautious for the rest of Gehennom.  Vlad fell quickly as did the
wizard.  The only tight spot occurred on the way back up when two
Wizards's appeared to double team her whilst she was wielding her
pick-axe.  After a long battle one of the wizards fell and she
realised that it might make more sense to wield her two swords again
instead of fighting using her pick-axe.  Sure enough the second wizard
then quickly fell.

A lot of sliding back down in Gehennom and then finally she ventured
back up through the dungeon.  A long time was spent exploring the
elemental planes until finally she emerged on the Astral plane.  She
was lucky enough to find the right alter the first time and then
suddenly... she was a goddess!
...
Clicked through too quickly to get the rest of my information (I was a
little tired at this point)  Was wielding +5 Excalibur and +2 Silver
Saber at the end.  Most armor was at +3/+4, SDSM, Cloak of Magic
Resistance, Boots of Speed, Gauntlets of Power... ac was -22 (used to
be -40 before I lost protection and my +5 Cloak was disintigrated when
I prayed in Gehennom)

This is my first ascension and second time past the quest... I think I
find the early game hardest!

